   "body": "> [!WARNING]\n> Copilot couldn't run its full agentic review because it didn't start before the timeout. Make sure your repository has a runner available, or add a `copilot-code-review.yml` file specifying one with the `runs-on` attribute. See the [docs](https://gh.io/AA11tgch) for more details.\n\n<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n## Copilot review overview\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [This comment states the code is using Playwright&#39;s `expect().toPass()` pattern, but the…](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/pull/343391#discussion_r4343349361) · New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nRefactors the Playwright helper that focuses the chat input by changing how a “best” input is selected and by replacing attempt-based polling with a timeout-based loop.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Optimized locator counting in `findVisibleChatInput` by hoisting `count()` out of the inner loop.\n- Changed `findVisibleChatInput` to return on the first visible match instead of scanning for the active element and keeping a fallback.\n- Replaced attempt-count polling with a `timeoutMs`-based polling loop and adjusted related call sites/timeouts.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| .agents/​skills/​launch/​playwrightScripts/​focus-chat-input.ts | Updates chat-input discovery/focus flow and refactors polling/timeout behavior. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Lite</sub>",
